  "passage": {
    "text": "One small farm cannot do everything alone. Modern machinery costs a lot of money, and buying fertilizer for one farm is expensive. So the farmers in a village decided to work together. They founded a cooperative. A cooperative is a group of farmers who share their resources. They buy supplies together, so the prices are lower. They also sell their products together, so they get better prices. Every member can vote at the meetings. Now the cooperative is going to build a new storage facility. A small producer is weak alone, but in a group he is stronger.",
